WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:06.480
Film Courage: What ruins the story for you?
Dui Jarrod, Filmmaker/Playwright: Inauthenticity. Is that how you say that?

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:12.240
Film Courage: Yeah. Dui: When
you know that it's not authentic

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:17.920
that is what really just
ruins uh a film or a story for me when

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.600
you know this
is not the exact example of what this

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.840
person would have done
felt or truly believed i think it just

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.199
takes it always just seems to take me
out of the piece that's when i

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:34.000
when i when i see it's not authentic is
it the acting or is it the writing how

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.440
the character is portrayed
i think it's a little bit of both um at

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.719
times
i recently saw a play on broadway where

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:45.200
a woman was dealing with a very
hard situation as far as her son and

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.760
trying to figure out where he was and
how he was

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.039
but i could also tell that the story
wasn't

00:00:51.039 --> 00:00:54.480
authentically written it didn't come
from an authentic place

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.680
i think the actors did a phenomenal job
with the material that she was given but

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:00.239
i feel
like they were trying to tell a story as

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:03.359
opposed to letting the story come from
within

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:07.280
i think all of us get stories all the
time and we want to go out and just tell

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.439
those different stories but i think the
ones

00:01:09.439 --> 00:01:12.479
that resonate the most they come from a
place

00:01:12.479 --> 00:01:16.159
of authenticity not saying it
necessarily has to be your story

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:20.240
but it has to just be authentic and if
it's authentic people will connect with

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.960
that
right there's always i mean especially

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.840
now there's a debate on
can someone really tell a story about

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.799
